# The demo with Qwen3.8-27B: extraction on a disposable rented GPU, everything else on this machine.
#
# `deploy/gpu/controller/demo.py up --model 3.8` rents one GPU in the named region family (EU by
# default), installs a pinned vLLM on it, serves Qwen3.8-27B with the arguments the GPU qualification
# measured — thinking off at the server — and holds an SSH tunnel to it on 127.0.0.1:18000. This
# profile points extraction at that tunnel and keeps embedding on the local Ollama, so a machine that
# cannot hold the 38 GB local default runs the same journey. `demo-qwen3.6.env` is the same node with
# the other model.
#
#     export GPUAI_API_KEY=<the gpu.ai control-plane key>
#     python3 deploy/gpu/controller/demo.py up --workdir ~/.taisce-demo --model 3.8 --check   # eligible offerings, nothing created
#     python3 deploy/gpu/controller/demo.py up --workdir ~/.taisce-demo --model 3.8           # holds the node; leave it running
#     export TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY="$(cat ~/.taisce-demo/api_key)"
#     make test-inference INFERENCE_PROFILE=demo-qwen3.8
#     python3 deploy/gpu/controller/demo.py down --workdir ~/.taisce-demo
#
# ── WHAT THE CORPUS SAID ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Measured 2026-09-11 on one RTX PRO 6000, vLLM 0.29.0, thinking off: 19 of 19 corpus cases, three
# attempts each, the same relations and refusals as the local default. About four seconds per
# extraction from a laptop through the tunnel. docs/36-extraction-models.md has the detail.
#
# ── READ THIS BEFORE USING IT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Conversation text leaves this machine. It crosses the SSH tunnel to a machine that the operator does
# not run: on `community` capacity a third party hosts it, on `secure` capacity a provider's
# data-centre partner does, and either way the text being extracted is in that machine's memory while
# it is processed. `up` logs which class it placed on. The product's claim that data stays on the
# operator's infrastructure does not hold under this profile. It is for made-up conversations.
#
# ── WHERE THE KEY IS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Not here. demo.py generates a bearer key per run, places it on the node over SSH, and the node
# refuses requests without it; it dies with the node. It lives in the workdir, which demo.py refuses to
# place inside a Git worktree. It reaches generation only: embedding has its own endpoint and its own
# empty key, so the tunnel's key is never sent to Ollama.
#
# ── WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO YET ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Compose. The tunnel listens on this machine's loopback, and a container here reaches the host
# through `host.docker.internal`, which under Colima is not the host's loopback. This profile is for
# the tools and the tests; running the stack against the node is a separate step.

TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT:-http://localhost:18000/v1}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL:-Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY:-}

TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT:-http://localhost:11434/v1}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-qwen3-embedding:4b-q8_0}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY:-}

# Both are this machine: the tunnel's near end and Ollama. Host and port, never a URL.
TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST:-localhost:18000,localhost:11434}
